{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david","id":1195787,"title":"Help developing a setting. Camp David","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-15T10:54:41-07:00","id":1195787,"title":"Help developing a setting. Camp David","content":"I am planning on starting a story set in the CWoD. It would be a coming of age story centered around a summer camp in the Everglades called Camp David. Throughout the story, the main characters would deal with the trials of the camp which include being hazed by the senior campers while dealing with the strange activity that happens in and around the camp. All of this comes to a head when the boys go on a &quot;rite of manhood&quot; by going into the wilderness surrounding the camp on a scavenger hunt that is held ever year by the senior campers for the &quot; New Bloods&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy plan for the story is to have elements of the World of Darkness manifest subtly at first and become more and more apparent once the boys actually enter the swamp itself. My question for you guys is what type of elements of the CWoD could fit in and around a summer camp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T11:35:09-07:00","id":1195799,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, I could see:<br /> Changing Breeds: Mokol\u00e9 (Mokol\u00e9-Mbembe), Bastet (Qualmi and Pumonca), Gurahl (Forest Walkers), Ananasi, Ronda (bullshark), Ratkin and Nagah could be found in the Everglades.<br /> <br /> Changeling, especially Inanimae too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T13:55:59-07:00","id":1195835,"title":"","content":"Im playing in one summer camp werewolf game and running one changeling game with a similar theme of summer camp coming of age and growing into ones true self. The difference is both these camps were established by their respective kinds to help prepare others and to teach them their own ways.<br /> <br /> If your setting is a everglade you could have various spirits play minor roles, an embodied spirit of the water could cause trouble or various cryptids/bygones. Hello Florida skunk ape and little green men from the mounds! A will o wisp may appear along with ball lightning and these could be spirits or Chimera trying to claim lives. Will your players become over time supernatural or strictly mortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:23:39-07:00","id":1195889,"title":"","content":"Good ideas so far. Speaking of Mokole, one of my ideas for a Mokole character is one that spends most of it's time in Lake David, the Lake the camp is built around. Old Moe, as the old croc is known, is extremely territorial of the lake and chases away campers who dare try to swim in it. The odd part, at least to the campers, is that once Old Moe is actually out of the lake, sunbathing or doing whatever, Moe is extremely docile. The Pcs find out about this docility after the toddler brother of one of the older campers wanders off and they later find him on the shore of the lake, sitting next to Moe, with Moe not even acting a bit aggressive.<br /> <br /> I wonder why a Mokole would chose to make it's home in a summer camp though? Most of the characters will be mortal but, I am considering doing a second cast of characters who are a Pack of Garou about to go on the Rite of Passage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T17:06:36-07:00","id":1195901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1195889#post1195889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why a Mokole would chose to make it's home in a summer camp though? Most of the characters will be mortal but, I am considering doing a second cast of characters who are a Pack of Garou about to go on the Rite of Passage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest solution is for the lake to be a wallow. Or the lake contains a threat which he can withstand but could be dangerous to human, thus why he Chase them for their safety.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:09:05-07:00","id":1195952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1195901#post1195901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simplest solution is for the lake to be a wallow. Or the lake contains a threat which he can withstand but could be dangerous to human, thus why he Chase them for their safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these ideas are pretty good. Another Changing Breed that shows up is a Homid Gurahl who appears in the camp as a storyteller as part of some kind of cultural education program on local Native tribes. The Gurahl is oddly fond of the campers and often sticks around long after the cultural education in his bear form and seemingly keeps an eye on the camp from any threats from the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Another idea i have for part of the climax is for the boys to stumble upon a Harold and Harold mining facility right in the middle of the swamp during their scavenger hunt. As it turns out, the senior campers left the flag right in the middle of the facility during a camp-sponsored field trip as a hazing prank for the &quot;New Bloods.&quot; The boys decided to break into the facility during night time and get the flag then. Of course, this ends in them getting caught, but not before seeing the militarized PENTEX security guards. I am wondering how PENTEX is gonna react to this scenario and how the characters could possibly escape ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:23:50-07:00","id":1195955,"title":"","content":"Giving a Mage player's perspective, I'd say having some seemingly nonsensical camp chant or ceremony turn out to be a secret Hermetic ritual could be fun. It could even be that &quot;our esteemed founder&quot; himself was a proud Hermetic trying to subtly teach the younger generations and try to form a nifty Node while he's at it.<br /> <br /> And then there's that stupid campfire story about the cloned velociraptor that escaped from a secret (Progenitor) laboratory. Timmy Cartwright <i>swears </i>he saw one, but it's all dumb and fake. Right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T06:59:01-07:00","id":1196037,"title":"","content":"The Hermetic Founder is a good idea. In fact, ny idea is for the campers to all be members of a Boy Scouts-like group called The Junior Foresters and this Hermetic could be the organizations founder. But, i wonder which OoH house would start an organization like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:40:52-07:00","id":1196047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1196037#post1196037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hermetic Founder is a good idea. In fact, ny idea is for the campers to all be members of a Boy Scouts-like group called The Junior Foresters and this Hermetic could be the organizations founder. But, i wonder which OoH house would start an organization like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>House Jerbiton, as the most Sleeper-focused of the Houses, would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:56:23-07:00","id":1196055,"title":"","content":"I'm also a little outside my comfort zone on this one, but I think a story about Wyrm-tainted camp food courtesy of PENTEX could be funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:58:13-07:00","id":1196057,"title":"","content":"Another element that could be included is: Ghost Story!<br /> <br /> Just [any direction best suited] of the camp there used to be an indian village. They were living in harmony with the land until one day they were attacked and exterminated [Rival Indian tribe or Vikings if the legends are true] and if you spend the night in that area, you can sometimes see them or hear them (possible Wraith link).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T10:39:04-07:00","id":1196117,"title":"","content":"Ironically, despite being the WoD's premiere organizations that have their fingers in every pie, I can't think of many ways to incorporate either the Technocracy or the Camarilla. The velociraptor thing is the best I've got for the former, and the latter is too city oriented. (Maybe a coterie of Gangrel skulking around the woods?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:29:08-07:00","id":1196143,"title":"","content":"I could see a Ventrue financing the camp as a anonymous benefactor, maybe even financing/sponsoring underprivileged kids from their home city. Good for taxes and good for the Masquerade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:37:32-07:00","id":1196347,"title":"","content":"Did anybody else think that this was going to be about the presidential retreat in Maryland?<br /> <br /> Anyway, for some reason I see there being Fomori in the Everglades. Maybe that means that Pentex is up to something there. So far, a number of people have made W:tA related suggestions. What is your favorite WoD lines? That might determine what you should focus on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:42:35-07:00","id":1196350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1196347#post1196347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anybody else think that this was going to be about the presidential retreat in Maryland?<br /> <br /> Anyway, for some reason I see there being Fomori in the Everglades. Maybe that means that Pentex is up to something there. So far, a number of people have made W:tA related suggestions. What is your favorite WoD lines? That might determine what you should focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am partial to Werewolf. But, i am getting interested in mage too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 03-16-2018, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:00:03-07:00","id":1196572,"title":"","content":"Besides Dryad teasing some of the older boys, i am wondering how the other types of inanime would interact with the Junior Forestrrs and the camp as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:33:53-07:00","id":1196581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1195889#post1195889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why a Mokole would chose to make it's home in a summer camp though?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the bottom of the lake is a relic left over from the Age of the Dragon Kings (or whatever it is the Mokole call it; I often get their term confused with the one used in Exalted). <br /> <br /> As for the camp itself, there's always the idea of Shallowings, places where the barrier between the material world and the spirit world (umbra, shadowlands, dreaming, or other) is thinner/weaker than normal, sometimes to the point where normal people can cross over by accident, and it's much easier for spirit beings to materialize or otherwise act on the material world. <br /> <br /> And as far as the Everglades go, I recommend Marvel's old Man-Thing comics from the 1970s (if you can find online versions or the black &amp; white Essential reprints from.a few years ago). It has a lot of nice atmosphere and weirdness. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T19:30:58-07:00","id":1196685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1196581#post1196581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the bottom of the lake is a relic left over from the Age of the Dragon Kings (or whatever it is the Mokole call it; I often get their term confused with the one used in Exalted).<br /> <br /> As for the camp itself, there's always the idea of Shallowings, places where the barrier between the material world and the spirit world (umbra, shadowlands, dreaming, or other) is thinner/weaker than normal, sometimes to the point where normal people can cross over by accident, and it's much easier for spirit beings to materialize or otherwise act on the material world.<br /> <br /> And as far as the Everglades go, I recommend Marvel's old Man-Thing comics from the 1970s (if you can find online versions or the black &amp; white Essential reprints from.a few years ago). It has a lot of nice atmosphere and weirdness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThanks for the suggestions. Does it seem weird for the Mokole to be docile outside of the lake? Docile enough to let a toddler sit next to it. Also, I wonder what kind of operations Pentex would have in the Everglades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T20:18:33-07:00","id":1196698,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Mokole, it could just as well depend on his/her auspice. A Midnight Sun trickster or a Setting Sun warder may just have a soft spot for small children. <br /> <br /> As for PENTEX, in the southern half of the 'Glades, probably very little, as it's a pair of national parks/preserves (Everglades &amp; Big Cyprus). Northeast of that is apparently a water conservation area and a national wildlife refuge. The area just south of Lake Okeechobee is apparently an agricultural area, so they may have a sugarcane farm or the like owned by some agribusiness company. Beyond that, the most likely thing is property development around the edges near the big coastal urban/suburban areas. If you've never read any of Carl Hiaasan's novels, I highly recommend them to anyone wanting to set a game in southern Florida. Double Whammy is especially good for Werewolf related inspiration, as it involves a property development built on a former toxic waste dumping site. For your purposes, you may also get a bit of mileage out of his children's novel Hoot, which was made into a film a few years ago. <br /> <br /> (I will note, in regard to Man-Thing, that there could be an old Project Iliad lab abandoned out in the 'Glades somewhere. One were one of it's last failures is still lurking about ....) <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T20:03:18-07:00","id":1197015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1196698#post1196698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Mokole, it could just as well depend on his/her auspice. A Midnight Sun trickster or a Setting Sun warder may just have a soft spot for small children.<br /> <br /> As for PENTEX, in the southern half of the 'Glades, probably very little, as it's a pair of national parks/preserves (Everglades &amp; Big Cyprus). Northeast of that is apparently a water conservation area and a national wildlife refuge. The area just south of Lake Okeechobee is apparently an agricultural area, so they may have a sugarcane farm or the like owned by some agribusiness company. Beyond that, the most likely thing is property development around the edges near the big coastal urban/suburban areas. If you've never read any of Carl Hiaasan's novels, I highly recommend them to anyone wanting to set a game in southern Florida. Double Whammy is especially good for Werewolf related inspiration, as it involves a property development built on a former toxic waste dumping site. For your purposes, you may also get a bit of mileage out of his children's novel Hoot, which was made into a film a few years ago.<br /> <br /> (I will note, in regard to Man-Thing, that there could be an old Project Iliad lab abandoned out in the 'Glades somewhere. One were one of it's last failures is still lurking about ....)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good ideas with PENTEX. The reason i asked that question is because one part of the story i have planned is for the main characters to stumble upon a Pentex op while on a scavenger hunt and have them discover that someone put the last idem on the list, a Camp David flag, right in the middle of the site. So, the boys end up attempting to sneak onto the site in order to get it, only to get caught, but not before seeing a &quot;really ugly man&quot; in the sugar cane field. I am wondering how Pentex would react to this situation after learning that the boys saw one of their Fomori?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 03-18-2018, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:07:17-07:00","id":1197131,"title":"","content":"I guess it would depend on how much is seen.<br /> <br /> A Pentex employee could come by and threaten a lawsuit for trespassing...especially if this happens again. At the same time evaluating how much they know and whether a strike is requiered or not.<br /> <br /> Pentex could say &quot;The hell with it!&quot; and send a stike team. Giving the opportunity for the Mokol\u00e9 and Gurahl to shine.<br /> <br /> If efficient time elapse between the threat and the strike, the pissed-off Ventrue benefactor might send some security guard to avoid issues with &quot;his&quot; wards and &quot;his&quot; charity. A few well armed ghouls might suffise (especially if the camp staff had a ghoul or two (war veteran cook for example) maybe with a gangrel or Brujah (or 3) &quot;off-camera&quot; for heavy support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:27:49-07:00","id":1197163,"title":"","content":"If there <i>is </i>something at the bottom of the lake, I could imagine that the Technocracy might also show some interest in it. Maybe even to the point of trying to get some Void Engineers to put away their damn lasers and actually attempt to be subtle enough to infiltrate the camp staff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:04:12-07:00","id":1197173,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of PENTEX threatening to sue the camp. With the First Team, i'd think they'd send in a extraction one to kidnap the main characters if they'd learn too much. Also, since the Characters are minors and not shapechangers, i can see Pentex pinching a few pennies and sending two or three First members instead of a whole squad. Because, why waste money sending a whole squad just to kidnap a few Junior Foresters from a isolated summer camp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:11:29-07:00","id":1197636,"title":"","content":"Pentex could use one of their lovely mockery breeds for this or even a fomori animal. Especially if they want to make the big old gator to look bad and help a PR campaign about 'relocating' the scaly creature. Nothing spooks kids more then gator attacks and taking of lives or maiming, and delirium would probably make them think it was a big gator if its scaly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:14:56-07:00","id":1197639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195787-help-developing-a-setting-camp-david?p=1197636#post1197636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex could use one of their lovely mockery breeds for this or even a fomori animal. Especially if they want to make the big old gator to look bad and help a PR campaign about 'relocating' the scaly creature. Nothing spooks kids more then gator attacks and taking of lives or maiming, and delirium would probably make them think it was a big gator if its scaly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mockery Breeds, you say? Now that you mention it, the cabins <i>do </i>seem to have a roach problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}